# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# An .ics file MUST use CRLF line endings — RFC 5545 §3.1 makes it part of the
# format, not a platform convention. The `* text=auto` rule above would normalise
# out/calendar.ics to LF on the way into the repo, and the failure is completely
# silent: build-ics.ts keeps writing correct CRLF to disk and reporting success
# every day, while the bytes GitHub actually serves to a subscribed calendar
# client are malformed. Verified with `git add --renormalize`, which stripped all
# 347 CRs from a calendar that had been committed correctly before this file
# existed.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions, so the file
# round-trips byte-exact.
*.ics -text
